{% comment %}
  Per-order purchase limits: independently managed from customer limits.

  These limits are separate from customer-order-limit-config.liquid. A product
  may have either limit, both limits, or neither. Changing or removing a row here
  never changes the per-customer allowance or its refresh window.

  Each row takes two values:

    order_limit_handle   Either an exact EasyStore product handle/SKU, or a
                         trailing-wildcard family such as `MTG-HOB-*`. Matching
                         is case-insensitive after normalization.
    order_limit_maximum  units of each matched SKU allowed in one order/cart. 0
                         or a missing row leaves the product unlimited per order.

  Matching precedence is deterministic and does not depend on row order:

    1. An exact handle/SKU match wins over every wildcard family.
    2. Otherwise the longest matching wildcard prefix wins.

  That means a broad family can set a default and exact rows can override it:

    {% raw %}{% include 'per-order-limit-row', order_limit_handle: 'MTG-HOB-*', order_limit_maximum: 2 %}{% endraw %}
    {% raw %}{% include 'per-order-limit-row', order_limit_handle: 'MTG-HOB-CBB-EN-CASE6', order_limit_maximum: 1 %}{% endraw %}

  Multiple families can be added as separate rows. Only a single trailing `*` is
  supported; embedded wildcards and regex-style expressions are ignored by the
  storefront validator so a typo cannot unexpectedly match a wider range.

  The wildcard applies the same limit independently to every matched SKU. It is
  not a pooled/group allowance across the entire family.

  Examples are documentation only. Keep active business values below this
  comment; customer-wide limits remain in customer-order-limit-config.liquid.
{% endcomment %}
